---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Navbar from '../../components/Navbar.astro';
import PageShell from '../../components/PageShell.astro';
---

<Layout 
    title="Medical Disclaimer | Real BMI"
    description="Review the Real BMI medical disclaimer. Our calculators offer educational health estimates based on WHO & CDC references and are not diagnostic tools."
    canonicalURL="https://realbmicalculator.com/en/disclaimer/"
>
    <Navbar />
    <PageShell
      title="Medical Disclaimer"
      eyebrow="Important health notice"
      description="Understand how Real BMI provides educational health estimates and why you should consult a qualified professional for medical decisions."
      returnUrl="/en/"
      returnLabel="Home"
    >
      <div class="space-y-8 prose prose-zinc dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-[var(--muted-foreground)] leading-relaxed text-base sm:text-lg font-medium opacity-90">
        
        <p class="text-lg sm:text-xl font-normal text-[var(--foreground)] leading-relaxed">
          The health tools, charts, and articles on <strong>Real BMI</strong> are built for learning and personal awareness only. They help you check basic body numbers at home.
        </p>

        <!-- 1. What Real BMI Is -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            What Real BMI Is
          </h2>
          <p>
            Real BMI is a free digital health tool set. We offer:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5">
            <li>Body mass estimates based on published formulas from the WHO and CDC.</li>
            <li>Simple 3D body models that help you see your body shape.</li>
            <li>Standard health charts to help you check your numbers against public guides.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 2. What Real BMI Is Not -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            What Real BMI Is Not
          </h2>
          <p>
            Real BMI is not a clinic or hospital. We do not offer medical care:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong>Not Medical Advice:</strong> Our scores are not clinical checks or treatment plans.</li>
            <li><strong>Not a Diagnostic Tool:</strong> Only a doctor can diagnose health problems like heart disease or diabetes.</li>
            <li><strong>Not a Diet Plan:</strong> You should never start extreme diets or stop your pills based on calculator scores.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 3. Who Should Consult a Doctor -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Who Should Consult a Doctor
          </h2>
          <p>
            We urge you to talk with a licensed doctor or dietitian if you:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5">
            <li>Plan to lose or gain a large amount of body weight.</li>
            <li>Live with long-term conditions like diabetes, high blood pressure, or heart trouble.</li>
            <li>Are pregnant, nursing, or recovering from surgery.</li>
            <li>Have had an eating disorder or struggle with body image.</li>
            <li>Notice quick, sudden shifts in your body weight.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 4. Emergency Situations (Callout Box) -->
        <div class="p-5 sm:p-6 rounded-2xl bg-amber-500/10 border border-amber-500/30 text-[var(--foreground)] space-y-2 not-prose">
          <div class="flex items-center gap-2 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-xs sm:text-sm">
            <svg class="w-5 h-5 shrink-0" fill="none" viewBox="0 0 24 24" stroke="currentColor">
              <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M12 9v2m0 4h.01m-6.938 4h13.856c1.54 0 2.502-1.667 1.732-3L13.732 4c-.77-1.333-2.694-1.333-3.464 0L3.34 16c-.77 1.333.192 3 1.732 3z"/>
            </svg>
            Emergency Situations
          </div>
          <h3 class="text-base sm:text-lg font-bold text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Immediate Medical Assistance
          </h3>
          <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-[var(--muted-foreground)] font-medium">
            Real BMI is not made for medical emergencies. If you have chest pain, shortness of breath, sudden dizziness, or bad weakness, call 911 or 112 right away. You can also go to the nearest emergency room.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 5. BMI Limitations -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            BMI Limitations
          </h2>
          <p>
            Standard BMI has known limits that you should keep in mind:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong>Body Makeup:</strong> BMI compares weight to height. It cannot tell muscle from fat. An athlete with dense muscle can show a high BMI score even with very low body fat.</li>
            <li><strong>Age and Muscle Loss:</strong> Older adults often lose muscle as they age. This loss can hide body fat under a normal BMI score.</li>
            <li><strong>Ethnic Background:</strong> Body fat patterns differ across world groups. The WHO uses lower risk points for Asian adults (23.0 instead of 25.0).</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 6. Privacy: No Personal Health Information Stored -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Privacy: No Personal Health Information Stored
          </h2>
          <p>
            Your health numbers stay private to you:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong>Runs in Your Browser:</strong> All calculations run directly on your own device using local JavaScript.</li>
            <li><strong>No Tracking:</strong> We never save, store, or share your height, weight, age, or waist numbers on our servers.</li>
            <li><strong>No Public Profiles:</strong> Real BMI does not have public user lists or message boards where your data could be seen.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 7. Legal Disclaimer -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Legal Disclaimer &amp; Limitation of Liability
          </h2>
          <p>
            Real BMI and its creators take no legal blame for choices you make based on this site. You use these tools of your own free choice and at your own risk.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 8. Special Clinical Situations: Pregnancy, Pediatric Growth & Sarcopenia -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Special Clinical Situations: Pregnancy, Pediatric Growth &amp; Sarcopenia
          </h2>
          <p>
            Standard BMI ranges apply only to non-pregnant adults aged 18 to 65. Certain groups need special care from a doctor:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-1.5">
            <li><strong>Pregnancy:</strong> In singleton pregnancies, healthy weight gain depends on pre-pregnancy BMI. Sudden weight gain or severe swelling can point to preeclampsia. This is a serious condition that requires prompt obstetric care.</li>
            <li><strong>Children and Teens:</strong> Growing children must never be judged using adult BMI cutoffs. A pediatrician should check their growth using CDC growth charts.</li>
            <li><strong>Older Adults:</strong> In seniors, muscle loss (sarcopenia) can mask fat gains. A slightly higher BMI between 23.0 and 27.9 often protects against bone breaks in seniors.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <!-- 9. Lifestyle Screening Guide vs. Clinical Diagnostic Evaluation -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Lifestyle Screening Guide vs. Clinical Diagnostic Evaluation
          </h2>
          <p>
            Each tool on this site is a lifestyle screening guide, not a medical test. Only a doctor can diagnose health issues like high blood pressure, diabetes, or heart risks.
          </p>
          <p>
            All 23 computational health tools on Real BMI provide helpful estimates. They help you ask good questions at your next doctor visit.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 10. Medication, Severe Caloric Restriction & Extreme Fitness Risks -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Medication, Severe Caloric Restriction &amp; Extreme Fitness Risks
          </h2>
          <p>
            If you take prescription medicine, like insulin, blood pressure pills, or thyroid pills, do not change your dose based on web tools. Weight changes can alter how your body processes pills.
          </p>
          <p>
            Also, eating under 1,200 calories per day without a doctor's care carries real health risks. It can lead to low energy, gallstones, and muscle loss. Always ask a doctor before you make big diet cuts.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 11. Laboratory Biomarkers & Holistic Clinical Diagnostics -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Laboratory Biomarkers &amp; Holistic Clinical Diagnostics
          </h2>
          <p>
            Numbers like BMI and body fat are starting points. True heart health needs lab tests done in a clinic.
          </p>
          <p>
            We urge you to get regular checkups. Your doctor can test your fasting blood sugar, HbA1c, and cholesterol levels. They will also check your resting blood pressure. Real BMI supports doctor visits, but never replaces them.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- 12. Verification Standards & Professional Inquiries -->
        <div class="space-y-2">
          <h2 class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-display font-bold uppercase tracking-tight text-[var(--foreground)]">
            Verification Standards &amp; Professional Inquiries
          </h2>
          <p>
            Real BMI is managed by software engineer <strong>Bhawanshi Dosi</strong> in Banswara, Rajasthan, India. All formulas match public papers from the WHO and CDC.
          </p>
          <p>
            If you have questions or want to verify a formula, reach us through our <a href="/en/contact/" class="text-[var(--accent)] underline font-medium">contact page</a>.
          </p>
        </div>

      </div>
    </PageShell>
</Layout>
